Existing host-check inventory (preserved, not run during the October 2026 refactor)

- auto_cool_test.cpp: portable hysteresis, trend, recovery, and cancellation.
- temperature_history_test.cpp / temperature_history_api_test.cpp: ring/cursors,
  gaps, bounded pages, and formatting.
- web_dispatch_test.cpp: threaded handoff, priority, generations, cancellation.
- test_auto_cool_integration.py: extracted AC integration with fake IR/NVS.
- test_web_async.py: fake HTTP transport and main-loop handoff integration.
- test_web_ui.js: browser polling, ordering, history, and lamp edit behavior.
- test_lotus_protocol.py: portable packet parsing/encoding, optional Python reference.
- test_lotus_worker.py: actual worker source compiled against dependency fakes;
  brought forward from the earlier session, with final latch changes unverified.

Migration is deferred, not complete. Native headers moved to
lib/ControllerCore/src and lib/ControllerWeb/src. Python/JavaScript scripts still
refer to the old src paths, inline web_ui.h, and/or functions extracted from
main.cpp. Update them to the new class interfaces and web/ sources before reuse;
BLE fakes also need the split worker/session and teardown API. No replacement
tests were written or run for this refactor. README.md contains native compiler
commands using the new include paths; those commands are not claimed to have
been rerun.

No on-device validation was performed. Host fakes and firmware build sizes cannot
prove IR reception, electrical stability, Wi-Fi/BLE behavior, or runtime heap and
stack safety. See README.md for the runtime limitations.
